"""
BASE Squidiff leakage test on sci-Plex (A/B/C protocol).
Adapted from the user's training_2 leakage script. Runs THREE protocols on the
SAME (drug x cell_line) conditions:

  A) control_feature = TREATED cell  + drug fp -> decode  [reconstruction-flavored]
  B) control_feature = CONTROL cell  + drug fp -> decode  [genuine prediction = trained mode]
  C) control-mean baseline (no model)

KEY DIFFERENCE FROM THE PLUS-VARIANT SCRIPTS (annotated):
  The BASE encoder.forward overwrites x_start with concat([control_feature, drug_dose])
  whenever drug_dose is provided (verified in MLPModel.py). So:
    - x_start is IGNORED (passed as a dummy of correct shape).
    - the treated-vs-control swap goes through CONTROL_FEATURE, not x_start.
    - there is NO cell_id / cell-line embedding in the base (no CELL_LINE_TO_ID needed).
  This is the reverse of the plus-variant framing: here Protocol B (control_feature=control)
  is the IN-DISTRIBUTION / trained mode, and Protocol A (control_feature=treated) is the
  artificial reconstruction probe.

Per-condition R2 and Pearson on mean expression, aggregated to E[.], per cell line.
GPU needed (decoder runs). model_0.9999.pt (EMA) to match convention.
"""
